    // ------------------------------------------------------------------------- exterior, §13.7 --
    // The thirteen outdoor regions of the plot, plus `EXT_WORLD` for everything beyond the fences.
    // They sit on `L0` because grade is where they are; rule 2 exempts an `exterior` cell from the
    // ceiling bound (its ceiling is the sky) and the floor bound does not bite because the
    // basement is under the main block only, and none of these are.
    //
    // §13.7 marks its extents "Approximate", and they are: eleven pairs of them overlap, by up to
    // 133 m², and two overlap the porch. This task resolved them into an exact tiling and that
    // resolution is a decision, not a transcription. The rules used:
    //
    //   * a region named as being inside another is CARVED OUT of it, not laid over it -- the
    //     shed out of the garden, the garden out of the west side yard, the terrace and the
    //     orchard out of the back lawn;
    //   * the side yards are the strips outboard of everything else and run the full depth of the
    //     plot, so the boundary between "side yard" and "back lawn" is the building line;
    //   * every region stops at a building face rather than running under one.
    //
    // Measured after the resolution: **no overlap anywhere, and the thirteen regions plus the four
    // building footprints tile the whole plot X -22.5…+22.5, Z -52…+13.4 with nothing left over.**
